  "notes": "Symphonic-goth pop-rock with a classically-trained lead: the singles sit 88–97 straight with the backbeat on 2&4 and the ballads at 57–74, both straight, so a single window carries 57–97. Harmony is E minor and other natural minors running i–VI–III–VII and i–iv–VI \"with a piano-voiced minor-add9; **no modulation, no dominant**\", so no authored family contains a V and the ninth share is the highest in this batch. Three drum deltas are quoted: \"kick 1 and the '&' of 2 with double-kick 16ths under the riff\" — a 3–7 density, the busiest kick in the section — \"snare 2&4 with a huge room\" (a loud accent tier), and \"china-crash accents\" with \"timpani and orchestral bass drum used for the fills\", which is the crash/tom/tomLow perc block and an 8-bar big-fill schedule. The bass is \"drop-tuned distorted electric bass locked to the kick; the piano's left hand doubles it an octave up\", which is `mirror_kick` at 0.96 with the register floor at MIDI 26 and the chord voicing lifted to 45 so the bass stays under it. The lead is documented as A3–D5 and \"operatic-legato in the verse and belted in the chorus\", and the piano is \"the primary melodic instrument, answered by a wall of down-tuned guitars\" — which is why the countermelody sits an octave *below* the lead as an answer lick. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are every drum probability; the entry names placements, rooms and instruments, not values.",
